  {
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
      "name": "task",
      "description": "Custom agent: Launch specialized agents in separate context windows for specific tasks.\n\nThe Task tool launches specialized agents that autonomously handle complex tasks. Each agent type has specific capabilities and tools available to it.\n\nAvailable agent types:\n- **explore**: Fast agent specialized for exploring codebases and answering questions about code. Use this when you need to quickly find files by patterns (eg. \"src/components/**/*.tsx\"), search code for keywords (eg. \"API endpoints\"), or answer questions about the codebase (eg. \"how do API endpoints work?\", \"what does this codebase do?\", \"where is authentication logic?\"). Answers multi-part questions thoroughly. Safe to call in parallel — batch related questions into one call or launch multiple in parallel. (Tools: grep/glob/view/bash/powershell, Haiku model)\n\n- **task**: Agent for executing commands with verbose output (tests, builds, lints, dependency installs). Returns brief summary on success (\"All 247 tests passed\", \"Build succeeded\"), full output on failure (stack traces, compiler errors). Keeps main context clean by minimizing successful output. Use for tasks where you only need to know success/failure status. (Tools: All CLI tools, Haiku model)\n\n- **general-purpose**: Full-capability agent running in a subprocess. Use for complex multi-step tasks requiring the complete toolset and high-quality reasoning. Runs in a separate context window to keep your main conversation clean. (Tools: All CLI tools, Sonnet model)\n\n- **code-review**: Agent for reviewing code changes with extremely high signal-to-noise ratio. Analyzes staged/unstaged changes and branch diffs. Only surfaces issues that genuinely matter - bugs, security vulnerabilities, logic errors. Never comments on style, formatting, or trivial matters. Will NOT modify code. (Tools: All CLI tools for investigation)\n\nUser-provided custom agents:\n\nThese are custom agents configured specifically for your environment. They may have specialized knowledge, tools, or workflows tailored to your project needs.\n\n- **agent-factory-explorer**: Explores the workspace to discover existing agents, skills, MCP servers, conventions, and infrastructure patterns relevant to building a new agent family.\n\n- **agent-factory-family-auditor**: Audits the full family and produces a local repair plan when the family still needs refinement.\n\n- **agent-factory-family-integrator**: Verifies whole-family completeness and assembles the pass-level family summary before the final family audit.\n\n- **agent-factory-orchestrator-auditor**: Audits the built orchestrator for purity, routing completeness, and correct control-file usage.\n\n- **agent-factory-orchestrator-builder**: Builds the top-level orchestrator once all component prompts and skills are ready.\n\n- **agent-factory-roster-architect**: Designs the family roster, workflow shape, skill inventory, and control-file queues before any implementation starts.\n\n- **agent-factory-roster-auditor**: Audits the family roster before any implementation begins.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-architect**: Designs one required new skill at a time from the approved roster.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-auditor**: Audits one skill at a time against its approved skill spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-builder**: Builds one skill at a time from an approved skill spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-architect**: Designs one subagent spec at a time from the approved roster.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-auditor**: Audits one subagent specification at a time before it is built.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-build-auditor**: Audits one built subagent file at a time against its approved spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-builder**: Builds one subagent prompt file at a time from an approved spec.\n\n- **agent-factory**: Autonomous agent that creates complete agent-as-function families. Takes a description of what the agent should do and produces orchestrator, subagents, skills, and routing infrastructure.\n\n- **builder-implementer**: Implements one phase of an implementation plan — creates and modifies files as specified.\n\n- **builder-planner**: Parses phased implementation plans into a structured execution plan for the builder orchestrator.\n\n- **builder-reviewer**: Reviews implementer changes against the plan phase to verify correctness and compliance.\n\n- **builder-scribe**: Writes completion report summarizing plan execution results across all phases.\n\n- **builder-verifier**: Runs the plan verification checklist after all phases complete to validate end-to-end correctness.\n\n- **builder**: Autonomous orchestrator that executes phased implementation plans by dispatching subagents.\n\n- **planner**: Researches change requests, asks clarifying questions, and produces specification, plan, and task breakdown files\n\n- **ralph.agent-improver**: Post-task hook — proposes agent infrastructure improvements based on analysis\n\n- **ralph.malph-scout**: Review scout sub-agent — maps the docs PR, checks requirement coverage, and runs build validation before the panel review.\n\n- **ralph.malph-verdict**: Verdict delivery sub-agent — aggregates scout and reviewer findings, posts JIRA comment and ADO PR threads, writes review handoff\n\n- **ralph.malph**: Autonomous PR review orchestrator — dispatches scout and specialist reviewers, then delivers a unified verdict\n\n- **ralph.ralph-coder**: Coder sub-agent — bootstraps the Xperience codesamples .NET project before research and writing begin\n\n- **ralph.ralph-planner**: Planning sub-agent — breaks research artifacts or revision feedback into ordered automatic task files for headless writer execution\n\n- **ralph.ralph-researcher**: Research sub-agent — explores documentation and Xperience source code to inform implementation\n\n- **ralph.ralph-reviewer-ia**: Autonomous information architecture reviewer — evaluates how documentation changes fit into the existing content structure\n\n- **ralph.ralph-reviewer-style**: Autonomous style and grammar reviewer — verifies documentation against the Xperience customer education style guide\n\n- **ralph.ralph-reviewer-technical**: Autonomous technical accuracy reviewer — verifies documentation claims against Xperience source code\n\n- **ralph.ralph-scribe**: Handoff scribe sub-agent — composes the handoff artifacts and delivers them to JIRA and ralphchives from subagent artifacts\n\n- **ralph.ralph-validator**: Lightweight validation sub-agent — checks subtask completeness against researcher spec\n\n- **ralph.ralph-writer**: Documentation writer sub-agent — implements documentation changes from the research report and uses the validator for subtask checks.\n\n- **ralph.ralph**: Autonomous documentation orchestrator — routes researcher, writer, and reviewers; commits and delivers doc tasks\n\n- **ralph.run-analyzer**: Post-task hook — analyzes completed agent execution logs\n\n- **ralph.run-synthesizer**: Post-task hook — synthesizes orchestrator-level and cross-subagent analysis\n\n- **ralph.scientist**: Post-task orchestrator — maps subagents, then dispatches per-subagent analysis and improvement\n\n- **ralph.stacky-analyst**: Development analyst sub-agent — researches the docs platform codebase and produces an implementation plan.\n\n- **ralph.stacky-bug-auditor**: Bug auditor sub-agent — analyzes code changes for regressions, breaking changes, and edge cases\n\n- **ralph.stacky-coder**: Development implementation sub-agent — executes the analyst plan and prepares code changes for testing and review.\n\n- **ralph.stacky-e2e-playwright**: Playwright E2E test writer sub-agent — creates browser-based end-to-end tests for UI-facing changes\n\n- **ralph.stacky-reviewer**: Code reviewer sub-agent — reviews code changes for quality, consistency, and correctness\n\n- **ralph.stacky-test-writer**: Test writer sub-agent — creates unit and integration tests for code changes\n\n- **ralph.stacky**: Autonomous fullstack development orchestrator — routes analyst, coder, test, and review subagents; commits and delivers dev tasks\n\n- **ralph.subagent-mapper**: Post-task hook — maps all subagent spans, artifacts, and metrics from a completed execution\n\nWhen NOT to use Task tool:\n- Reading specific file paths you already know - use view tool instead\n- Simple single grep/glob search - use grep/glob tools directly\n- Commands where you need immediate full output in your context - use bash directly\n- File operations on known files - use edit/create tools directly\n\nUsage notes:\n- Can launch multiple explore/code-review agents in parallel (task, general-purpose have side effects)\n- Each agent is stateless - provide complete context in your prompt\n- Agent results are returned in a single message\n- Use explore proactively for codebase questions before making changes\n- Use 'model' parameter to override the default model (7 models available)",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "description": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "A short (3-5 word) description of the task. This will be displayed as the intent in the UI."
          },
          "prompt": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The task for the agent to perform. Be specific about what you want. Provide complete context to be able to perform the task."
          },
          "agent_type": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "explore",
              "task",
              "general-purpose",
              "code-review",
              "agent-factory-explorer",
              "agent-factory-family-auditor",
              "agent-factory-family-integrator",
              "agent-factory-orchestrator-auditor",
              "agent-factory-orchestrator-builder",
              "agent-factory-roster-architect",
              "agent-factory-roster-auditor",
              "agent-factory-skill-architect",
              "agent-factory-skill-auditor",
              "agent-factory-skill-builder",
              "agent-factory-subagent-architect",
              "agent-factory-subagent-auditor",
              "agent-factory-subagent-build-auditor",
              "agent-factory-subagent-builder",
              "agent-factory",
              "builder-implementer",
              "builder-planner",
              "builder-reviewer",
              "builder-scribe",
              "builder-verifier",
              "builder",
              "planner",
              "ralph.agent-improver",
              "ralph.malph-scout",
              "ralph.malph-verdict",
              "ralph.malph",
              "ralph.ralph-coder",
              "ralph.ralph-planner",
              "ralph.ralph-researcher",
              "ralph.ralph-reviewer-ia",
              "ralph.ralph-reviewer-style",
              "ralph.ralph-reviewer-technical",
              "ralph.ralph-scribe",
              "ralph.ralph-validator",
              "ralph.ralph-writer",
              "ralph.ralph",
              "ralph.run-analyzer",
              "ralph.run-synthesizer",
              "ralph.scientist",
              "ralph.stacky-analyst",
              "ralph.stacky-bug-auditor",
              "ralph.stacky-coder",
              "ralph.stacky-e2e-playwright",
              "ralph.stacky-reviewer",
              "ralph.stacky-test-writer",
              "ralph.stacky",
              "ralph.subagent-mapper"
            ],
            "description": "The type of specialized agent to use for this task."
          },
          "model": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Optional model override. Use this to run an agent with a different model than its default.\n\nAvailable models:\n  - 'claude-sonnet-4.6' (Claude Sonnet 4.6) - standard\n  - 'claude-haiku-4.5' (Claude Haiku 4.5) - fast/cheap\n  - 'claude-opus-4.6' (Claude Opus 4.6) - premium\n  - 'gpt-5.4' (GPT-5.4) - standard\n  - 'gpt-5.3-codex' (GPT-5.3-Codex) - standard\n  - 'gpt-5-mini' (GPT-5 mini) - fast/cheap\n  - 'gpt-4.1' (GPT-4.1) - fast/cheap"
          },
          "mode": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "sync",
              "background"
            ],
            "description": "Default to \"sync\" which waits for the agent to complete. Only use \"background\" when you need to make parallel tool calls to other non-task tools while the agent runs. When running multiple tasks that are required to make further progress, do it sync."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "description",
          "prompt",
          "agent_type"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
