        "content": "Perfect! Now I have comprehensive information. Let me create a complete summary with all the file paths and key details.\n\n---\n\n## Summary: ralph-reviewer-technical Configuration & Behavior\n\nI've located and read all the key configuration files for the `ralph-reviewer-technical` subagent. Here's the complete picture:\n\n### **File Locations**\n\n| File | Path |\n|---|---|\n| **Technical Reviewer Prompt** | `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph-reviewer-technical.agent.md` |\n| **Main Orchestrator (Ralph)** | `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph.agent.md` |\n| **Artifact Contract (Execution Model)** | `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/agent-as-function-contract.md` |\n| **Review Phase Reference** | `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/workflow/docs/ralph-workflow/references/4-review.md` |\n| **Xperience Source Skill** | `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/xperience/SKILL.md` |\n| **Source References Skill** | `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/integrations/ralph-source-references/SKILL.md` |\n| **Codesamples Reviewer Include** | `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/ralph-docs/ralph-codesamples-reviewer.md` |\n\n---\n\n### **1. Technical Reviewer Configuration**\n\n**Model:** Claude Opus 4.6\n\n**Key Directives:**\n- **Autonomous operation** — makes judgment calls independently; never uses `ask_questions` or requests human input\n- **Review-only** — does NOT edit files; writes only to artifact directory\n- **Adversarial reviewer mindset** — assumes every technical claim is wrong until verified against source code\n- **Strict, no rubber-stamping** — one unverified claim triggers rejection\n\n**Result Codes:**\n- `approved` — all technical claims are accurate or reasonably simplified\n- `needs-revision` — specific technical inaccuracies found with evidence\n\n---\n\n### **2. Expected Tools & Skills**\n\nThe reviewer references and uses:\n\n| Skill/Tool | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `xperience` | Source-map router for CMSSolution; identifies subsystem ownership before deep verification |\n| `ralph-source-references` | Generates source browser URLs for citing Xperience source code locations |\n| `ralph-codesamples-verification` | (Optional) Verifies added code samples work at runtime; used only when needed |\n\n**Access to:**\n- `resources/repositories/xperience/` — Xperience by Kentico C# source code (gitignored; use `includeIgnoredFiles: true`)\n- `src/_code/src/` — Code examples used in documentation\n- `src/_documentation/` — Documentation pages (for cross-reference if needed)\n\n---\n\n### **3. Dispatch Instructions (from Ralph Orchestrator)**\n\n**When Dispatched:**\nThe main orchestrator (`ralph.ralph.agent.md`) dispatches `ralph-reviewer-technical` as part of a **three-reviewer gate** after the writer completes a task.\n\n| Condition | Action |\n|---|---|\n| Writer completes a task (`task-implemented` or `all-tasks-implemented`) | Dispatch all three reviewers: technical, style, IA |\n| Any reviewer returns `needs-revision` | Re-dispatch writer to fix; then re-run **only** failing reviewers (max 3 revision cycles per task) |\n| All three reviewers return `approved` | Proceed to next task or to commit phase |\n\n**Dispatch Flow (from Phase 4-5 Reference):**\n1. Orchestrator invokes all three reviewers simultaneously with the current task ID\n2. Each reviewer reads:\n   - Planner task file (`ralph-planner/task-*.md`)\n   - Writer's latest output (`ralph-writer/output-v{N}.md`)\n   - Actual changed files from the diff\n3. Reviewer returns `status.json` with verdict code\n4. Orchestrator aggregates: **all three must approve** or task goes back to writer\n5. Maximum **3 revision cycles** per task; after that, proceeds with \"not converged\" note\n\n---\n\n### **4. Verification Checklist**\n\nThe reviewer **must verify** for each touched file:\n\n**API Accuracy:**\n- [ ] Class names, method signatures, property names match source code\n- [ ] Parameter types and names are correct\n- [ ] Return types accurately described\n- [ ] Generic type parameter names match (`<T>` vs `<TItem>` etc.)\n\n**Configuration & Values:**\n- [ ] Enum values and option names accurate\n- [ ] Default configuration values match source\n- [ ] Environment variable names correct\n- [ ] Connection string formats valid\n\n**Behavioral Claims:**\n- [ ] Described behavior matches actual implementation\n- [ ] Sequence of operations correct\n- [ ] Error conditions and edge cases accurately documented\n- [ ] Lifecycle hooks fire in documented order\n\n**Code Samples (if included):**\n- [ ] Code uses current, non-deprecated APIs\n- [ ] `code_link` paths match actual file locations under `src/_code/src/`\n- [ ] Build passes (`npm run codesamples:build`)\n- [ ] Sample organization follows feature-folder conventions\n- [ ] `//Include:` / `//EndInclude:` markers wrap intended code regions\n- [ ] No `Generated/` folder edits\n- [ ] New objects have `codesamples.` codename prefix\n- [ ] No needless data seeders (seeders only for transactional data)\n\n**Inheritance & Architecture:**\n- [ ] Class hierarchies and interface implementations correct\n- [ ] Abstract vs concrete class distinctions accurate\n- [ ] Dependency injection registrations match source\n\n---\n\n### **5. Evidence Standard (CRITICAL)**\n\nFor every finding, the reviewer **MUST** provide:\n\n1. **Exact documentation quote** that is inaccurate\n2. **Actual source code** with namespace, class, and method\n3. **Source browser URL** in format:\n   ```\n   https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#<CMS.Namespace/Path/ClassName.cs>,<LineNumber>\n   ```\n\n**Important:** URLs must use fully-qualified .NET namespace starting with `CMS.` prefix, not filesystem paths.\n\nExample: \n- Wrong: `https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#DbDataManager/Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs,222`\n- Correct: `https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#CMS.DbDataManager/Installation/SqlInstallationHelper.cs,222`\n\n---\n\n### **6. Output Format**\n\n**Primary Artifact:** `{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-technical/output-v{N}.md`\n\n```markdown\n## Technical Accuracy Review\n\n**Assessment:** APPROVED | NEEDS REVISION\n**Task:** TASK-XX — <task title>\n\n### Verified ✅\n- `Namespace.ClassName.Method()` — accurately documented\n  Source: [ClassName.cs:45](https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#CMS.Namespace/ClassName.cs,45)\n\n### Inaccuracies ⚠️ (if any)\n\n#### ACC-001: [Brief description]\n**Severity:** Critical | Minor\n**Location:** [File, section/line]\n**Documentation says:** \"[exact quote]\"\n**Source shows:** `[actual API/value]`\n**Evidence:** [ClassName.cs:120](https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#CMS.Namespace/ClassName.cs,120)\n**Fix:** [Exact correction needed]\n\n### Could Not Verify ❓\n- [Claims where source was inconclusive]\n\n### Summary\n- Verified: X claims\n- Inaccuracies: Y findings\n- Unverifiable: Z claims\n- **Recommendation:** APPROVED | NEEDS REVISION\n```\n\n**Structured Findings:** `review-findings.json`\n```json\n{\n  \"reviewer\": \"ralph-reviewer-technical\",\n  \"verdict\": \"approved|needs-revision\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"code\": \"ACC-001\",\n      \"path\": \"src/_documentation/...\",\n      \"summary\": \"Technical inaccuracy summary\",\n      \"fix\": \"Exact correction needed\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Status File:** `status.json` (artifact contract)\n```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"ralph-reviewer-technical\",\n  \"task_id\": \"{{ taskId }}\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"result\": \"approved|needs-revision\",\n  \"summary\": \"<one line, ~100 tokens>\",\n  \"artifacts\": [\"ralph-reviewer-technical/output-v{N}.md\"],\n  \"iteration\": 1\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **7. Scope Boundaries**\n\n- **In scope:** Only changes in current planner task and files touched by that task\n- **Out of scope:** Existing inaccuracies in surrounding untouched content (unless the change makes them worse)\n- **Reasonable simplification acceptable** — documentation doesn't need 1:1 mirror of source; flag genuine inaccuracies, not omissions for brevity\n- **No invented findings** — if can't find evidence of inaccuracy, report it under \"Could Not Verify\"\n\n---\n\n### **8. Revision Review Context**\n\nWhen this is a **revision review** (fixing issues from a previous round), the reviewer:\n- Focuses on whether **technical feedback items were addressed**\n- Confirms **no new inaccuracies** were introduced by fixes\n- Is lenient on pre-existing issues unrelated to revision feedback\n- Does NOT re-verify previously-approved claims unless fixes touched them\n\n---\n\n### **9. Severity Classification**\n\nAll findings must be classified as:\n- **Critical:** Genuine technical inaccuracy blocking approval\n- **Minor:** Imprecise wording; technically correct but could confuse advanced users\n\n---\n\n### **10. Artifact Contract (Execution Model)**\n\nThe reviewer operates as a **subagent** communicating via filesystem artifacts:\n- Orchestrator reads **only** `status.json` for routing decisions\n- Reviewer writes versioned output (`output-v{N}.md`) for iteration tracking\n- Must append entry to `manifest.json` after writing `status.json` (audit trail)\n- Conversational return: Single line — `Done. Status: {status}, result: {result}.`",
