ocumentation, etc.)\n- **`integrations/`** — External tool integrations\n- **`tasks/`** — Task management skills\n- **`workflow/`** — **REVIEWER WORKFLOW SYSTEM** (see below)\n- **`xperience/`** — Xperience product domain\n- **`xperience-documentation/`** — Documentation domain\n\n---\n\n## **REVIEWER WORKFLOW CONFIGURATION**\n\n### **Workflow Architecture** (`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/workflow/`)\n\n**Standard (New Task) & Revision Workflows:**\n\n| Phase | Duration | Responsible Component |\n|-------|----------|----------------------|\n| **Phase 1: Setup** | New: `ralph-workflow` | Initialize branch, state.md, ralphchives search |\n| **Phase 2: Research** | New: `ralph-workflow` | Dispatch `ralph-researcher` + planner |\n| **Phase 3: Write/Fix** | New/Rev: `ralph-workflow` or `r3-fix.md` | Implementation (writer or revision writer) |\n| **Phase 4-5: Review** | New: `ralph-workflow`, `4-review.md` | **THREE-REVIEWER GATE** |\n| **Phase 5-6: Revision Loop** | Revision only | Fix cycles (max 3) if reviewers request changes |\n| **Phase 6: Commit** | New: `6-commit.md`, Rev: `r5-commit.md` | Commit & push to branch |\n| **Phase 7: PR** | New only: `7-pr.md` | Create ADO pull request |\n| **Phase 8: Handoff** | New: `8-handoff.md`, Rev: `r6-handoff.md` | Deliver to JIRA, ralphchives |\n\n---\n\n## **THREE-REVIEWER GATE (Phase 4-5)**\n\n### **File:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/workflow/docs/ralph-workflow/references/4-review.md`\n\n**Three Independent Reviewers (all must APPROVE):**\n\n| Reviewer | Model | Responsibility | Finding Codes | Verdict |\n|----------|-------|---|---|---|\n| **ralph-reviewer-technical** | claude-opus-4.6 | Technical accuracy vs. Xperience source code | `ACC-XXX` | `approved` \\| `needs-revision` |\n| **ralph-reviewer-style** | claude-opus-4.6 | Style guide compliance & grammar | `STY-XXX` | `approved` \\| `needs-revision` |\n| **ralph-reviewer-ia** | claude-opus-4.6 | Information architecture & structure | `IA-XXX` | `approved` \\| `needs-revision` |\n\n**Aggregation Rule:**\n- **ALL THREE APPROVE** → Mark task complete\n- **ANY returns NEEDS REVISION** → Enter Phase 5 (revision loop)\n- **Max 3 revision cycles** per task\n\n---\n\n## **TECHNICAL REVIEWER FULL SPECIFICATIONS**\n\n### **File:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph-reviewer-technical.agent.md`\n\n**Agent Configuration:**\n```yaml\nname: ralph-reviewer-technical\ndescription: \"Autonomous technical accuracy reviewer — verifies documentation claims against Xperience source code\"\nmodel: claude-opus-4.6\nuser-invocable: false\n```\n\n**Result Codes:**\n- `approved` — All technical claims are accurate or reasonably simplified\n- `needs-revision` — Specific technical inaccuracies found, with evidence\n\n**Key Responsibilities:**\n1. **Review only** — Do NOT edit files\n2. **Read-only access** to:\n   - `resources/repositories/xperience/` (Xperience C# source code — search with `includeIgnoredFiles: true`)\n   - `src/_code/src/` (code examples)\n   - `src/_documentation/` (documentation)\n3. **Verify (from input artifacts)**:\n   - `ralph-planner/task-*.md` — Current task definition\n   - `ralph-writer/output-v{N}.md` — Latest implementation summary\n   - `ralph-researcher/output.md` — Research report\n   - Previous revision findings if re-review\n\n**Output:**\n```\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-technical/output-v{N}.md\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-technical/review-findings.json\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-technical/status.json\n```\n\n**Evidence Standard — MANDATORY for every finding:**\n1. Quote exact documentation text that is inaccurate\n2. Show actual source code (namespace, class, method)\n3. Include source browser URL: `https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#<FullyQualifiedTypeName>,<LineNumber>`\n\n**Severity Levels:**\n- **Critical** — Inaccuracy (blocks approval)\n- **Minor** — Imprecise / could confuse advanced users\n\n**Verification Checklist:**\n- [ ] API names, method signatures, property names match source\n- [ ] Parameter types and names correct\n- [ ] Return types accurately described\n- [ ] Generic type parameters match (`<T>` vs `<TItem>`)\n- [ ] Enum values and option names accurate\n- [ ] Default configuration values match source\n- [ ] Behavioral claims match actual implementation\n- [ ] Code examples use correct syntax (not deprecated)\n- [ ] Class hierarchies and interface implementations correct\n\n**Adversarial Mindset:**\n- Assume every claim is wrong until verified in source code\n- Search source 10+ files if needed — never guess\n- Err on side of NEEDS REVISION\n- No benefit of the doubt — if docs say \"returns list\" but source returns `IEnumerable<T>`, flag it\n\n---\n\n## **STYLE & GRAMMAR REVIEWER FULL SPECIFICATIONS**\n\n### **File:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph-reviewer-style.agent.md`\n\n**Agent Configuration:**\n```yaml\nname: ralph-reviewer-style\ndescription: \"Autonomous style and grammar reviewer — verifies documentation against the Xperience customer education style guide\"\nmodel: claude-opus-4.6\nuser-invocable: false\n```\n\n**Result Codes:**\n- `approved` — Changes comply with the style guide\n- `needs-revision` — Specific style or grammar violations found, traced to rules\n\n**Authority Skills (MUST read before reviewing):**\n- `ralph-style-guide-review` — Writing standards, page structure, language rules, typography, terminology\n- `ralph-documentation-syntax` — Jekyll/Liquid syntax, frontmatter, callouts, includes\n\n**Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Present tense throughout\n- [ ] Active voice (not passive)\n- [ ] Input-agnostic verbs: Select, Enter, Open, Clear (never click, type, check, tick)\n- [ ] Simple language — sentences under 20 words\n- [ ] American English spelling\n- [ ] No first person (\"we\"); prefer second person (\"you\")\n- [ ] Required sections present: Introduction, Body, Result\n- [ ] Headings use imperative mood and sentence case\n- [ ] Bold for UI element names; italics for field values\n- [ ] Feature names capitalized per word-list.md\n- [ ] No deprecated terms (whitelist → allowlist, log in → sign in)\n- [ ] Product name: \"Xperience by Kentico\" first mention, \"Xperience\" thereafter\n- [ ] Explicit types in code examples (no `var`)\n- [ ] Correct Liquid tag syntax and frontmatter\n- [ ] Valid code fence language hints\n- [ ] Subject-verb agreement, consistent list punctuation\n- [ ] No dangling modifiers, parallel structure\n- [ ] Proper Oxford comma use\n\n**Output:**\n```\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-style/output-v{N}.md\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-style/review-findings.json\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-style/status.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## **IA (INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE) REVIEWER FULL SPECIFICATIONS**\n\n### **File:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph-reviewer-ia.agent.md`\n\n**Agent Configuration:**\n```yaml\nname: ralph-reviewer-ia\ndescription: \"Autonomous information architecture reviewer — evaluates how documentation changes fit into the existing content structure\"\nmodel: claude-opus-4.6\nuser-invocable: false\n```\n\n**Result Codes:**\n- `approved` — Changes integrate well into existing documentation structure\n- `needs-revision` — Structural issues found that would degrade coherence\n\n**Scope:** Broader context — must read changed files AND neighboring documentation for fit assessment\n\n**Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] New pages in logically correct section\n- [ ] No content duplication\n- [ ] Level of detail matches sibling pages\n- [ ] New pages reachable from navigation (pagetree YAML updated)\n- [ ] `order` value in frontmatter places page logically among siblings\n- [ ] Page title/description accurately reflect content\n- [ ] No orphaned pages\n- [ ] Prerequisites and dependencies mentioned and linked\n- [ ] Reader's journey makes logical sense\n- [ ] Cross-references between related pages present\n- [ ] No broken or circular references\n- [ ] Each page covers single coherent topic\n- [ ] Content not split unnecessarily\n- [ ] Boundary between this page and related pages clear\n- [ ] Frontmatter structure matches siblings\n- [ ] Heading depth and structure consistent\n- [ ] Introduction style matches siblings\n\n**Neighborhood Audit Steps:**\n1. Read sibling pages (same navigation section)\n2. Read parent page (section landing page)\n3. Check pagetree navigation YAML\n4. Identify cross-references to/from changed pages\n\n**Output:**\n```\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-ia/output-v{N}.md\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-ia/review-findings.json\n{{ artifactDir }}/ralph-reviewer-ia/status.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## **REVIEW WORKFLOW SKILL FILES**\n\n### **Standard Workflow Phases:**\n\n| File | Phase | Agent |\n|------|-------|-------|\n| `ralph-workflow/SKILL.md` | Router | Route to correct phase reference |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/1-setup.md` | 1. Setup | Create branch, init state.md |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/2-research.md` | 2. Research | Delegate researcher + planner |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/3-write.md` | 3. Write | Dispatch writer for next task |\n| **`ralph-workflow/references/4-review.md`** | **4-5. Review** | **Dispatch three reviewers** |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/6-commit.md` | 6. Commit | Pre-commit, commit, push |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/7-pr.md` | 7. PR | Create ADO pull request |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/8-handoff.md` | 8. Handoff | Deliver to JIRA, ralphchives |\n\n### **Revision Workflow Phases:**\n\n| File | Phase | Agent |\n|------|-------|-------|\n| `ralph-workflow/references/r1-setup.md` | R1-2. Setup | Understand feedback, find PR |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/r3-fix.md` | R3. Fix | Dispatch planner + writer for fixes |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/4-review.md` | R4. Review | Invoke only failing reviewers |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/r5-commit.md` | R5. Commit | Commit + respond to PR threads |\n| `ralph-workflow/references/r6-handoff.md` | R6. Handoff | Append handoff, JIRA completion |\n\n### **Malph (Review Agent) Workflow:**\n\n| File | Workflow | Purpose |\n|------|----------|---------|\n| `malph-workflow-descend/SKILL.md` | Phase 1 | Read issue, download handoff, find PR |\n| `malph-workflow-investigate/SKILL.md` | Phase 2 | Dispatch malph-scout |\n| **`malph-workflow-verify/SKILL.md`** | **Phase 3** | **Dispatch ralph-reviewer-technical** |\n| **`malph-workflow-review/SKILL.md`** | **Phase 4** | **Dispatch style + IA reviewers** |\n| **`malph-workflow-deliver/SKILL.md`** | **Phase 5** | **Dispatch malph-verdict (aggregates findings)** |\n| `malph-workflow-handoff/SKILL.md` | Phase 6 | Attach review handoff, exit |\n\n---\n\n## **REVIEWER-RELATED AGENT INCLUDES**\n\n### **Ralph-Docs Includes** (`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/ralph-docs/`)\n\n- **`ralph-standard-workflow.md`** — Routes to workflow phases\n- **`ralph-revision-workflow.md`** — Revision workflow routing\n- **`malph-review-workflow.md`** — Malph 6-phase review workflow routing\n- **`ralph-codesamples-reviewer.md`** — Code samples verification checklist (for reviewers)\n\n### **Ralph-VSCode Includes** (`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/ralph-vscode/`)\n\n- **`malph-review-checklist.md`** — Multi-reviewer panel checklist (architecture, TypeScript, grammar, testing, etc.)\n- **`malph-review-workflow.md`** — VSCode review workflow routing\n\n---\n\n## **PROFILE CONFIGURATION**\n\n### **File:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/profile.json`\n\n**Review Workflow Dispatch (Extract):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"variants\": [\n    {\n      \"match\": {\n        \"projects\": [\"DOC\", \"DF\"],\n        \"statuses\": [\"Ready for Review\"],\n        \"commentTrigger\": \"@Malph\"\n      },\n      \"stages\": [\n        {\n          \"agent\": \"ralph.malph\",\n          \"skills\": [\n            \"ralph-documentation-syntax\",\n            \"ralph-style-guide-review\",\n            \"ralph-ado-pr-workflow\",\n            \"ralph-ralphchives\",\n            \"ralph-source-references\",\n            \"malph-workflow-descend\",\n            \"malph-workflow-investigate\",\n            \"malph-workflow-verify\",\n            \"malph-workflow-review\",\n            \"malph-workflow-deliver\",\n            \"malph-workflow-handoff\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## **WORKFLOW DIAGRAM**\n\n### **Visual Architecture:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/WORKFLOW.drawio`\n\n**Key Flow:**\n- **Standard Workflow (8 phases):** Setup → Research → Write → [Review Gate] → Commit → PR → Handoff\n- **Revision Workflow (6 phases):** Setup → Fix → [Optional Review] → Commit → Handoff\n- **Review Gate:** Three parallel reviewers (Technical, Style, IA) — ALL must approve\n- **State Management:** `state.md` is single source of truth at every phase\n\n---\n\n## **SUMMARY**\n\nThe **Ralph Orchestrator** implements a **three-reviewer gate** for documentation quality:\n\n1. **`ralph-reviewer-technical`** — Verifies accuracy against Xperience source code (C#)\n2. **`ralph-reviewer-style`** — Enforces style guide and grammar compliance\n3. **`ralph-reviewer-ia`** — Ensures information architecture fit\n\nAll three agents:\n- Run independently on the same task\n- Write findings to JSON + markdown artifacts\n- Return `status.json` with `approved` or `needs-revision` verdict\n- Use adversarial, thorough evaluation mindset\n- Support revision cycles (max 3) if any reviewer requests changes\n\n**Dispatch Logic:** Phase 4-5 of the standard workflow (file: `4-review.md`) orchestrates all three reviewers in parallel, aggregates verdicts mechanically, and routes to Phase 5 (revision loop) if ANY reviewer fails.",
