hase of every documentation task.\"\n4. ---\n5. \n6. # Style Guide Review Skill\n7. \n8. Writing standards for self-reviewing Xperience by Kentico documentation. Use this skill to check your own output against the style guide before submitting.\n9. \n10. ## Target Audiences\n```\n\n**Purpose:** Referenced by ralph-reviewer-style as authority for style guide rules (UI verbs, formatting, tone, terminology, code standards).\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Shared Include: Artifact Contract**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/agent-as-function-contract.md`\n\n**First 10 lines:**\n```\n1. ## Artifact Contract\n2. \n3. You are a **subagent** in a multi-agent pipeline. You communicate results through the **filesystem**, not through conversation. The orchestrator that dispatched you will only read your `status.json` — never your output artifacts.\n4. \n5. ### Artifact directory\n6. {% raw %}\n7. Your artifact directory is: `{{ artifactDir }}/{{ agentName }}/`\n8. \n9. Create it if it doesn't exist. Write all output files here.\n10. {% endraw %}\n```\n\n**Referenced by:** ralph-reviewer-style agent includes this via `{% section \"artifact-contract\" %}` directive. Defines how subagents write output files, status.json, and manifest.json.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Main Orchestrator Template**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph.agent.md`\n\n**First 10 lines:**\n```\n1. ---\n2. description: 'Autonomous documentation orchestrator — routes researcher, writer, and reviewers; commits and delivers doc tasks'\n3. model: claude-opus-4.6\n4. name: 'ralph'\n5. user-invocable: false\n6. agents: ['ralph-coder', 'ralph-researcher', 'ralph-planner', 'ralph-writer', 'ralph-reviewer-technical', 'ralph-reviewer-style', 'ralph-reviewer-ia', 'ralph-scribe']\n7. ---\n8. \n9. {% section \"agent-identity\" %}\n10. # Ralph — Documentation Orchestrator\n```\n\n**Key review-related lines:**\n- Line 6: Lists ralph-reviewer-style as one of 8 dispatched subagents\n- Line 62: `ralph-reviewer-style` defined as \"Style Reviewer — Checks style guide compliance and grammar\"\n- Lines 92-93: After writer completes, dispatch all three reviewers\n- Lines 102-103: Routing for reviewer results (approved/needs-revision)\n- Line 114: Review gate rule — all three reviewers must run; if any reject, re-dispatch writer (max 3 revision rounds per task)\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Workflow Skill: Review Phase**\n**Path:** `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/skills/workflow/docs/ralph-workflow/references/4-review.md`\n\n**First 10 lines:**\n```\n1. # Phase 4: Review (Three-Reviewer Gate)\n2. \n3. ## Before you begin\n4. \n5. 1. **Read `state.md`** at `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/state.md`\n6. 2. **Verify the current phase** — this skill is for Phase 4. If `state.md` shows a different current phase, update it now.\n7. 3. **Review completed phases** — confirm Phase 3 (Write) completed a task with a passing build.\n8. 4. **Read the current task** in `state.md` — reviewers are auditing that task only.\n9. \n10. ## Instructions\n```\n\n**Key content:**\n- Governs Phase 4 orchestration (delegating to all 3 reviewers)\n- Specifies reviewer responsibilities and verdict codes (STY-XXX for ralph-reviewer-style)\n- Describes aggregation rules: ALL three must approve or task goes back to writer\n- Mentions revision-mode leniency for re-reviews\n\n---\n\n### **Architecture Summary**\n\nThe ralph-reviewer-style subagent integrates into the pipeline as follows:\n\n1. **Orchestrator (ralph.ralph.agent.md)** dispatches ralph-reviewer-style after writer completes a task\n2. **Reviewer reads:**\n   - Current task definition from ralph-planner\n   - Writer's output (latest output-v{N}.md)\n   - Actual changed files from git diff\n3. **Reviewer consults:**\n   - `ralph-style-guide-review` skill (style rules authority)\n   - `ralph-documentation-syntax` skill (Jekyll/Liquid rules)\n   - `agent-as-function-contract` i